## 2. Variable-Length (VL) Prefix Framing

Variable-length fields (`Blob`, `AccountID`, `Vector256`, `PublicKey`) prefix their payload with length octets:

* **1-Octet ($0 \dots 192$ bytes)**: Length is stored directly as a single byte.
* **2-Octets ($193 \dots 12480$ bytes)**:
  $$\text{byte}_0 = 193 + \left\lfloor \frac{\text{len} - 193}{256} \right\rfloor, \quad \text{byte}_1 = (\text{len} - 193) \pmod{256}$$
* **3-Octets ($12481 \dots 918744$ bytes)**:
  $$\text{byte}_0 = 241 + \left\lfloor \frac{\text{len} - 12481}{65536} \right\rfloor, \quad \text{byte}_1 \dots \text{byte}_2 = (\text{len} - 12481) \pmod{65536}$$

