## 3. Object and Array Terminators

`ObjectEndMarker` and `ArrayEndMarker` are protocol-definition entries for the
real nested-scope terminators. They are encoded by the ordinary field-ID
primitive rather than a separate serializer operation:

* `addFieldID(STI_OBJECT, 1)` combines type 14 and field 1 into `0xE1`.
* `addFieldID(STI_ARRAY, 1)` combines type 15 and field 1 into `0xF1`.

The object/array implementations append these bytes piecemeal after nested
payloads. A top-level object has no enclosing field and ends when its input is
exhausted, so it does not append an end marker for itself.
